During a relatively concentrated period of activity on LinkedIn, my writing and posts generated more than 20,000 impressions and reached approximately 7,800 members. Notably, 52% of those impressions came from outside my existing network. The activity also generated 96 comments, alongside reactions, saves, and reposts. I find this particularly relevant because my intention has been to communicate complex systems ideas in a way that people from different backgrounds can engage with, rather than limiting those discussions to a single technical discipline.
:::

:::writing{variant="standard" id="68312"}
I have also found that communicating these ideas in an accessible way has opened conversations with people from a variety of professional backgrounds, including technology, engineering, research, education, health, and other fields. That experience has reinforced my belief that addressing complex technological and societal challenges requires the ability to communicate across disciplines and learn from perspectives that may be very different from one's own.
:::
